      "writtenOn": "2023-02-16T10:32:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Your logic seems to be correct - `usb3_dut` will return state of the USB3 knob which you designed. But what about changing \"enabled\" to \"allowed\"? It is possibly correct that one issued `usb3_dut enable` but due to other reasons (e.g. pd stack state) usb3 is not really enabled.",
      "revId": "7e524d2d1b4680a51e94db69c14e22de68fd1de4",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8d0b4dde_99180b0e",
        "filename": "board/servo_v4p1/board.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 113,
      "author": {
        "id": 1520718
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-16T17:38:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Seems to be reasonable. I changed final information to user to \"allowed/enabled\" and also add extra note in command description. However I would like to stay with \"dut_usb3 enable\" as it is designed to always force USB3 enablement. If you issue this command, it turns off DUT hub, enable USB3 (no matter what), then turn on DUT hub, so new USB3 devices can be enumerated. It can be overwritten by some other logic later, but not just after command.  \n\nThis also forces small change in servod part of mechanism, but I will do it when this CL would be ready.",
      "parentUuid": "ee6fffba_af4b4c6e",
      "revId": "7e524d2d1b4680a51e94db69c14e22de68fd1de4",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
