        "id": 1421833
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-16T10:32:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So basically for a short period USB3 (terminations) will be enabled and only then we will get back to disabling them? Won\u0027t this cause any issues for the host connected to the servo? Is similar functionality used for other boards?",
      "revId": "7e524d2d1b4680a51e94db69c14e22de68fd1de4",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "383a7c9e_d54cfc7a",
        "filename": "board/servo_v4p1/board.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 139,
      "author": {
        "id": 1520718
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-16T17:38:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Indeed MUX for short moment enables USB3 then disables. In my test no issues were spotted, but it is possible that some of them can occur later. What I can propose is to make sure DUT hub is disconnected then set MUX and finally enable DUT hub witch will start enumeration process. For sure its safer and should not introduce any additional problems. It does not in my tests on desk.",
      "parentUuid": "38e72108_cb683bd6",
      "revId": "7e524d2d1b4680a51e94db69c14e22de68fd1de4",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
